    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d870">

                <pb facs="0827" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/818</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1917-12-15T20:46:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1917-12-15T19:00:00-05:00" when="1917-12-15"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received December 15, 1917, 8.46
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1186. My 1175. I have just been informed by the British Legation here that the
                    attitude of the British Government in recognizing the independence of Finland is
                    that as soon as a properly constituted Russian Government recognizes the
                    independence of Finland the British Government is prepared to do the same.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
